==Rules==
{{StageRule|12thAnni}}

==Battleground==
*15 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 33.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*4 [[Puffzerker]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Before even attempting the stage, consider running the best Health Up [[Cat Combo]]s you have available to you. Otherwise, even at Lv.50, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] will have immense trouble landing hits against Professor A. It is also recommended to upgrade your [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]'s Cost Down and HP Buff [[Talents|Talents]] to as high of a level as you can; without Ubers, you'll need at least 40,000¢ to get by without running out of cash midway through.

The pushing power of these enemies is unimaginable, and they will aim to overwhelm you in extreme numbers. Try to rush this stage as quickly as you can with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]]/[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]], Courier Cats, and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]]. If you own Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] by this point, he will be invaluable in chunking Professor A. and Two Can alongside the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] Cannon every so often.

'''Don't even bother with {{2c}} until you have at least 55,000¢, especially if you don't have the strongest anti-Red Ubers.''' Boosting Roe Cat to high +levels is of utmost importance to survive, but even that won't be nearly enough to hold off the onslaught. The strategy for {{1c}} won't work at all this time around, so your new goal should be to kill Two Can as fast as humanly possible using well-timed rushers like Courier Cat, Neo Cutter Cat and Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat (equip an Attack Up Orb vs. Red on him if you must). This is to prevent any more incoming units from getting sniped to death. Once he's dead, you're free to deploy any backliners/superbackliners you have, e.g. [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]], to clean up the crowd. From that point going forward, there's nothing that can really threaten you outside of your own financial status (just like real life), so try to conserve as much cash as you possibly can while your backliners slowly take care of things.

